activation	Compute current body text	2026-10-20T07:32:14.7748744Z text: INTERNAL ERROR code that is not equivalent to the source (non-UTF8, iso-8859-1)\n\n\n**Describe the bug**\n\nHistoric behaviour:\n\n```\n❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\nblack, 23.9.1 (compiled: no)\nPython (CPython) 3.13.5\nAll done! ✨ 🍰 ✨\n1 file would be left unchanged.\n```\n\n```\n❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\nblack, 25.12.0 (compiled: no)\nPython (CPython) 3.13.5\nAll done! ✨ 🍰 ✨\n1 file would be left unchanged.\n```\n\nNew behaviour:\n\n```\n❯ black --version && black --diff tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\nblack, 26.1.0 (compiled: no)\nPython (CPython) 3.13.5\nerror: cannot format tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py: INTERNAL ERROR: Black 26.1.0 on Python (CPython) 3.13.5 produced code that is not equivalent to the source.  Please report a bug on (github/redacted)[.]com/psf/black/issues.  This diff might be helpful: /var/folders/_b/zf5p80v11bd2m2fq4j17z8mr0000gn/T/blk_9jeg_ijj.log\n\nOh no! 💥 💔 💥\n1 file would fail to reformat.\n```\n\n```\n❯ cat  /var/folders/_b/zf5p80v11bd2m2fq4j17z8mr0000gn/T/blk_9jeg_ijj.log\n--- src\n+++ dst\n@@ -63,11 +63,11 @@\n                 value=\n                 Constant(\n                     kind=\n                     None,  # NoneType\n                     value=\n-                    'Initialize name instance.\n\n>>> fred = Name("FrÃ©dÃ©ric", "FranÃ§ois")\n>>> print(fred)',  # str\n+                    'Initialize name instance.\n\n>>> fred = Name("FrÃ\x83Â\x83Ã\x82Â©dÃ\x83Â\x83Ã\x82Â©ric", "FranÃ\x83Â\x83Ã\x82Â§ois")\n>>> print(fred)',  # str\n                 )  # /Constant\n             )  # /Expr\n             Assign(\n                 targets=\n                 Attribute(\n```\n\nLooks like a change in how non ASCII strings are represented?\n\n**To Reproduce**\n\nUsing this file: (github/redacted)[.]com/peterjc/flake8-rst-docstrings/blob/master/tests/test_cases/not_utf8.py\n\nThis is a test case over five years old, as per the file header:\n\n> This file is not using UTF-8, but Western European.\n>\n> It works fine using the Windows-1252 or iso-8859-1 encoding,\nbut not using UTF-8 which is the Python default.\n\n**Expected behavior**\n\nNo error, no reformatting as in black 23.9.1 or black 25.12.0\n\n**Environment**\n\n- Black's version:  26.1.0\n- OS and Python version: macOS / Python 3.13.5 \n\n**Additional context**\n\nSpotted by CI under Linux, see (github/redacted)[.]com/peterjc/flake8-rst-docstrings/pull/102
